//! Reference interpreter of RDNA 2 programs (wave32 and wave64): the Rust port of
//! `PrototypeScarlett/emu/rdna2_exec.py`. The Python stays the oracle: `tests/test_rdna2_ref_parity.py`
//! runs the same programs through both and compares the final state, instruction by instruction.
//!
//! Done: the decoder (`decode`, with the mnemonic table `mnemonics`, generated by
//! `tools/rdna2_ref_tables.py` from `emu/rdna2_ops.py`), the wave state (`wave`), the scalar
//! instructions and the branches (`scalar`, `exec`), the vector families (`vector`, `compare`, `vop3`,
//! `vop3p`, ...), the sparse global memory (`memory`), the scalar memory (`smem`) and the integer
//! atomics (`atomic`). Not yet: the LDS, buffer, FLAT and GLOBAL memory, the typed formats, images and
//! graphics; they refuse with `Error::Untranslated`.

